# shell: both
# The operation's own lifecycle is a fact: idle, then idle again with
# the copies there.  The mid-flight claim is not made even here: the
# engine steps on a worker now, and three small files are copied
# between two turns -- bigcopy.script, with a file large enough to be
# caught in flight, makes that claim.
wait 12
expect-operation idle
key a ctrl
wait 3
key c ctrl
wait 3
key v ctrl
note mid-flight the job speaks its count -- the one phrase every
note caption shares and idle never says
expect-operation idle
expect-read /tmp/trk_script a.txt copy
quit
